## Removed optimization machinery

- **3-layer hash system** (`hashNodeInputs`, `hashSelfPaths`, field-path
hashing) — evaluation skip detection
- **Trigger-scoped walks** — partial DAG walks based on watch event
routing
- **Per-node resync timers** — exponential backoff, jittered resync
- **Worker goroutine dispatch** — channel-based coordinator with Path
1/2/3 logic
- **ForEach incremental item diffing** — per-item content hash caching,
changed-item sets
- **Watch incremental cache** — `mergeCollectionChanges`, collection
dirty tracking
- **Evaluation caching** — `previousEvalHashes`, `previousSelfHashes`,
`snapshotFor`

## What replaced it

Simple sequential DAG walk: for each node in topological order, check
dependencies → includeWhen → propagateWhen → evaluate → publish to
scope. No goroutines, no channels, no hash checks. Every node is
evaluated every reconcile (correct by construction).

